<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Leopold I, Prince of Lippe</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1767">1767</a>–<a href="/years/1802">1802</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Leopold I was count and, from 1789, the first prince of Lippe, a small state in north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>. He took up the princely rank granted to the family earlier in the century, turning the County of Lippe-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/detmold">Detmold</a> into the Principality of Lippe. After his death in 1802 his widow Pauline governed as regent until 1820.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/leopold-i-prince-of-lippe.jpg" alt="Leopold I, Prince of Lippe" width="320" height="400" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Leopold_I._F%C3%BCrst_zur_Lippe.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
